# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# C930 SoC FIT-TEST flow for ECP5 (oss-cad-suite Yosys).
#
# Same flow as synth.ys, but with the two caches shrunk via chparam
# (INDEX_WIDTH 7 -> 3, i.e. 128 -> 8 lines) so the netlist fits the
# ECP5-85F fabric and nextpnr can place-and-route it for an Fmax number.
# (INDEX_WIDTH 4 was tried first: 76K LUTs = 90% of the fabric, and the
# router could not finish at that density.)
#
# WHY: the full design as-synthesized is ~424K LUTs (511% of ECP5-85F) because
# the dcache's per-bit byte-strobe/AMO write muxes demote to ~366K LUTs (see
# synth.log). The fit test measures the LOGIC FABRIC (core + NPU + bridge +
# DMA) Fmax; it is NOT the real design's Fmax -- the caches must be re-architected
# to EBR (registered reads / native byte-enables) before the real design fits.
#
# The DDR placeholder (c930_ddr_stub.sv) is used instead of the blackbox
# because nextpnr cannot place blackboxes.
#
# chparam re-evaluates the parameterized MODULE (defaults are overridden at the
# top instantiation), which is why the cache geometry is parameterized through
# riscv_core_top (ICACHE_INDEX_WIDTH / DCACHE_INDEX_WIDTH).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

chparam -set ICACHE_INDEX_WIDTH 3 riscv_core_top
chparam -set DCACHE_INDEX_WIDTH 3 riscv_core_top

synth_ecp5 -top c930_soc_top -noabc9 -latches warn -run begin:map_luts

abc -lut 4 -script synth/light.abc

techmap -map +/lattice/latches_map.v
techmap -map +/lattice/cells_map_trellis.v
opt_lut_ins -tech lattice
clean

autoname
hierarchy -check
stat
check -noinit
blackbox =A:whitebox

write_json build/synth/fit.json
